From 068327c7bbc012a9689d48debf27f3660273678e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:31:41 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] policy, udc, urs: protect declared and foreign gadgets

usb-signaller disables and removes whatever gadget holds the UDC when it
switches modes, when it falls back to charging_only on SIGTERM and when
it switches to host role. That destroys gadgets other components rely
on, for example an initramfs gadget that serves the root filesystem over
USB: the root disappears and the device hangs.

Add [gadget.<dir>] tables that declare such gadgets, with
pinned_functions (merged as a union, so a later file can never silently
unpin anything) plus adopt, config, keep_identity and allowed_modes,
which are validated now and used by in-place management later. Unknown
keys in these tables make the configuration broken, so a typo cannot
drop a pin. [main] foreign_gadgets = "replace" (the default, today's
behaviour) or "preserve" decides what happens to gadgets that are
neither owned (usb-signaller-*) nor declared.

A declared gadget, or a preserved foreign one, holding the UDC makes
set_mode fail with "UDC <udc> is held by <declared|foreign> gadget <g>;
not replacing it" before any USB role is written, and the SIGTERM
cleanup leaves it without a single configfs write. host_mode is refused
before the role is written while a declared gadget with pins is bound,
or while the configuration is broken and a gadget usb-signaller does not
own is bound. A broken configuration declares nothing and preserves
every non-owned gadget, and (as before) applies no default mode.

The host role cleanup now only removes owned gadgets and keeps going
when one removal fails. UDC::load finds the bound gadget through
/sys/class/udc/<udc>/function, tolerates foreign gadgets it cannot
parse, and no longer indexes configs[0]/functions[0] unchecked, which
panicked on a bound gadget without configuration strings.

Unknown keys under [main] stay allowed, for forward compatibility, but
are reported with a warning naming the file and listed by
--print-config: a typo such as foreign_gadget = "preserve" would
otherwise silently leave foreign_gadgets at "replace".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
