+++ b/README.md
@@ -93,6 +93,54 @@ that set each key and exits without touching D-Bus or USB. It exits with status
 
 - **default_mode** (String): defines which USB mode must be applied on startup, for example: `developer_mode`.
   Must be one of the USB modes below.
+- **foreign_gadgets** (String): what to do with a bound configfs gadget that
+  usb-signaller did not create (its directory does not start with
+  `usb-signaller-`) and that is not declared in a `[gadget.<dir>]` section:
+  - `replace` (default): disable and remove it when switching modes, as before.
+  - `preserve`: never touch it. Mode switches fail while it holds the UDC and
+    it is left alone on shutdown.
+
+### Section gadget.\<dir\>
+
+Declares a configfs gadget that someone else created, for example an
+initramfs whose gadget serves the root filesystem. `<dir>` is the directory
+name under `/sys/kernel/config/usb_gadget/`. usb-signaller never disables,
+removes or replaces a declared gadget:
+
+- `set_mode` fails with `UDC <udc> is held by declared gadget <dir>; not
+  replacing it` while the gadget holds the UDC, and no USB role is written.
+- On shutdown the gadget is left untouched.
+- Switching to host role only removes gadgets usb-signaller created.
+- `host_mode` is refused while a declared gadget with pinned functions is bound.
+
+Keys:
+
+- **pinned_functions** (list of strings): functions of the gadget, as
+  `<driver>.<instance>` (for example `ffs.smoo` or `acm.GS0`), that must stay
+  linked and bound. Pins from all files are combined: a later file can add
+  pins but never remove one. Mask the file that added a pin (a same-named
+  symlink to `/dev/null`) to drop it.
+- **adopt** (boolean, default `false`), **config** (string),
+  **keep_identity** (boolean, default `true`) and **allowed_modes** (list of
+  USB modes, combined across files by keeping only modes every file allows)
+  are reserved for managing a declared gadget in place. They are validated,
+  but a declared gadget is currently only protected.
+
+An empty `[gadget.<dir>]` section declares the gadget without pins. Any other
+key in this section, an invalid function or mode name, or a directory name
+starting with `usb-signaller-` makes the configuration broken.
+
+While the configuration is broken, nothing is declared and every gadget
+usb-signaller does not own is preserved, whatever `foreign_gadgets` says.
+`host_mode` is refused while such a gadget is bound.
+
+Example, written at boot by an initramfs to
+`/run/usb-signaller/usb-signaller.toml.d/50-console.toml`:
+
+```toml
+[gadget.g1]
+pinned_functions = ["acm.GS0"]
+```
 
 ### Section mass\_storage
 
